]633;D;0;\PS D:\repos\Bikini\BikiniGit> cd "D:\repos\Bikini\BikiniGit"; git commit -m "WIP: ImagesView indexed view with deterministic VendorArtCode lookup

- Created AlterImagesViewDeterministic.sql to rebuild ImagesView with SCHEMABINDING
- Replaced non-deterministic FORMAT() with deterministic RIGHT() + CAST() for art code padding
- Added unique clustered index on Id (required for indexed views)
- Added non-clustered index on VendorArtCode for fast lookups
- Updated ShopifyOrderEngine to use direct VendorArtCode lookup instead of parsing
- Simplified image lookup from complex multi-column filtering to simple indexed lookup

Benefits:
- ImagesView is now a materialized indexed view (like a table)
- VendorArtCode column is directly indexable (was blocked by FORMAT())
- Query: WHERE artCodes.Contains(iv.VendorArtCode) uses index efficiently
- Will benefit many other parts of codebase doing awkward image lookups

Known issue: Hit an exception during testing - will debug tomorrow

This indexed view approach will replace numerous inefficient image lookup patterns throughout the codebase."

